# The images built from THIS directory as their context: si-orchestrator (container/Dockerfile) and the updater
# (container/updater/Dockerfile). The orchestrator does `COPY . /app/` and needs the WHOLE solution at runtime:
# container/, engine/, launcher/, auth/, asset-profiling-*/, risk-analysis-detection/ and its own ENTRYPOINT script.
# So this file is a DENY-list: it names what must never be uploaded, and everything else goes.
#
# 🔴 IT ONCE OPENED WITH `*` PLUS AN ALLOWLIST written for the (now deleted) SI Analyzer image. Under those rules
# `COPY . /app/` copied neither the engine, nor the launcher, nor /app/container/Start-SIInContainer.ps1 -- the image's
# own ENTRYPOINT. Keep it a deny-list. Guarded by tests/pester/SI-ContainerTranscript.Tests.ps1 ("the orchestrator
# build context can still contain what the entrypoints need").
# ---- NEVER upload customer or runtime config to the ACR build service ----
# These carry real tenant values and secrets. This is the rule the original file was
# written for, and it does not relax.
**/*.custom.ps1
**/*.custom.json
**/*.custom.csv
**/*.custom.yaml
# A SHIPPED file must never carry a "custom" name: live 2026-10-02 Risk Analysis in a container died at start ("Could
# not find file '/app/risk-analysis-detection/riskscore.index.custom.csv'") because this rule kept the then-shipped risk
# index out of the image. Since 3.0 the shipped index is riskscore.index.locked.csv and riskscore.index.custom.csv is
# the customer's own rows, which reach the jobs through the customisation share like the other *.custom.* files.
# A test fails when a tracked file matches a pattern above without an exception line here.
**/config/
# The SHIPPED *.locked.json files under config/ are product, not customer config (no tenant value): the settings
# catalog the Pro settings layer validates against, the CMDB ownership and service model the Pro engines read.
# Live 2026-10-02: the Pro layer stopped every container run with "settings catalog not found:
# /app/config/settings.catalog.locked.json". Customer config (*.custom.*, the reference .ps1) stays out.
!config/*.locked.json
# The customer's other customisation files. They used to reach the FIRST image only (built from the install's folder)
# and vanished on the first update, whose image is built from the published archive. They now reach every job from the
# install's storage account at run time (container/_shared/SI-ContainerRunState.ps1), so the image never carries them:
# the first image and every update image behave the same.
asset-profiling-providers/*/CMDB.csv
**/RiskAnalysis_Queries_Custom.yaml
**/*.exclude.json
**/DATA/
internal/
demo/

# ---- run output: large, regenerated, and needed by neither image ----
logs/
output/
staging/
**/OUTPUT/

# #574: build output of the PDF builder library (engine/_shared/pdf/SI.Pdf.csproj, built by the web app) -- the engine
# image gets the PDF DLLs from container/Install-SIPdfLibrary.ps1, never from a developer's build folder
engine/_shared/pdf/bin/
engine/_shared/pdf/obj/
